[{:seon.task/name "one-home-per-helper"
  :seon.task/plan "Done; what exists. One home per helper: `seon.reader/line-starts` (text and its positions) is the one line-start index, called by seon.repl and seon.source; `seon.sock/write-line!` writes a line through sock's own write loop (EINTR retried, :epipe its declared answer), and seon.lib's copies (`write-all!`, `write-line!`) are gone; seon.intr's uncalled poll installer (install-poll*) and its alias of `seon.lib/SIGUSR1` are gone; `seon.contract/uncontracted` is the one 'function var with no :malli/schema' rule (seon.stage no longer re-derives it). Each was a pure move or delete."
