  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.reader-test/line-starts-are-each-lines-offset seon.repl-test/an-agent-repl-answers-what-a-clojure-repl-answers seon.source-test/import-then-write-back-is-a-zero-diff}}
 {:seon.task/name "real-mb-reads-what-macos-charges"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23). What existed: bin/check scale's root gauge, seon.lib/real-mb, read 398-404 MB for a root whose phys_footprint was 1,460 MB with the embedding model open, and 856 MB on Seon's own program without it (jolt/similar-finds-helpers-by-embedding). Cause, measured: real-mb summed the private and shared-now-private resident pages of the process's VM regions, and a fork turns the parent's pages copy-on-write, so they left the sum: a parent holding a 730 MB block read 76 MB after forking one child (its phys_footprint stayed 730 MB); root forks the fork server, so it read about a quarter of what it holds. The note that macOS's footprint overstates a forked child does not hold for the task's own ledger: a child read 3 MB at the fork and 43 MB after writing 30 MB of the shared block. Fixed: real-mb is the task's phys_footprint (task_info TASK_VM_INFO: private dirty pages, compressed ones included, what Activity Monitor and jetsam charge), for root, the fork server and each agent; native/probe.c answers the ledger only, and its region walk (~1.5 ms a read) is deleted. bin/check scale's need reads it."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.lib-test/the-memory-gauge-reads-what-macos-charges-across-a-fork}}]
